KG42.register("rules-9f867c6dee22c6f9ee656fbc",{"id":"49-residential_shared_storage_market::v141-c-R003","paper":"49-residential_shared_storage_market","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R003","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Price-signal coordination","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"Following capacity allocation, users may respond to electricity prices by purchasing more energy and charging SES at low prices and discharging SES at high prices. Scope: Energy buyers using SES in the proposed local P2P market. Condition: After SES capacity allocation; charging when the electricity price is low and discharging when it is high. Energy buyers may use SES and adjust their charging/discharging strategy according to the electricity price on the premise of meeting the current energy deficit. Scope: Energy buyers' price-responsive SES charging/discharging strategies in the proposed local P2P market. Condition: The current energy deficit is met.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.price_signal under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["coordination.price_signal"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"Energy buyers using SES in the proposed local P2P market. | Energy buyers' price-responsive SES charging/discharging strategies in the proposed local P2P market.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e002","v141-b-g02-e006"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Following capacity allocation, users may respond to electricity prices by purchasing more energy and charging SES at low prices and discharging SES at high prices. Scope: Energy buyers using SES in the proposed local P2P market. Condition: After SES capacity allocation; charging when the electricity price is low and discharging when it is high.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e002"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Energy buyers may use SES and adjust their charging/discharging strategy according to the electricity price on the premise of meeting the current energy deficit. Scope: Energy buyers' price-responsive SES charging/discharging strategies in the proposed local P2P market. Condition: The current energy deficit is met.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.price_signal"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e006"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e002","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p04-c2r3__v141-a-M01-participation","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2 System configuration","anchor_text":"ng result. The solid arrows present the P2P transaction between typical ir energy sellers and energy","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"The shared energy storage is implemented in our proposed P2P energy trading market, which is large-capacity energy storage and shared by multiple energy buyers. We assume the storage device has been invested and installed on the community side. In this paper, we just focus on the operational problem of shared energy storage. In our business model, the energy buyers can use the capacity of SES instead of equipping individual energy storage, which can save storage investment costs for energy buyers. After the capacity allocation, users can purchase more energy and charge SES when the electricity price is low and discharge SES when the price is high, thus reducing their energy costs."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e006","location":{"location_id":"src-4c60176b12-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.2 Energy buyers","anchor_text":"in the P2P transaction market or trade with power utility according to de the price signal. Energy s","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Energy buyers consist of participants who consume energy, e.g., residential community, business building, shopping mall. We consider the residential community in this paper. Modeling the behavior of residential energy consumers requires both financial and emotional factors, integrating the economic and motivational psychology[56]. Besides, the ideal model is not always consistent with the real-world situation. So we choose the energy cost, which is a conspicuous and acceptable criterion to model consumer behavior. Each energy buyer, whose goal is to minimize the expenditure on energy purchase, can buy energy from the P2P market or power grid depending on the price signal. Besides, multiple buyers share the capacity use right of the SES, which provides the buyers with more flexible energy consumption management. They can use SES and adjust their charging/discharging strategy according to the electricity price on the premise of meeting the current energy deficit. To simplify the problem and show the operation of our P2P market, the initial energy demand of each energy buyer is fixed."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"This rule introduces no decision variable of its own. The charging/discharging quantities and price symbols discussed in the source belong to the buyer and clearing formulations and are not declared in this frozen single-node coordination rule.","empty_theta_reason":"The rule supplies no numeric value, threshold, coefficient, or bound defining what counts as a low or high electricity price, and it declares no parameter for the current energy deficit or for the charging/discharging response."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.price_signal","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e002","quote":"After the capacity allocation, users can purchase more energy and charge SES when the electricity price is low and discharge SES when the price is high, thus reducing their energy costs."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e006","quote":"They can use SES and adjust their charging/discharging strategy according to the electricity price on the premise of meeting the current energy deficit."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"38eab232f15b0f1ce0f0a899ac789bc2d4476ffd57e78ecfbd5404e6860f4686","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The frozen rule is a qualitative behavioral/permission statement: after capacity allocation, users may purchase more energy and charge SES at low electricity prices and discharge at high prices, subject to meeting the current energy deficit. The supplied evidence contains no threshold defining low/high electricity prices and no equation or inequality expressing this price-responsive charging/discharging as a standalone coordination constraint. The only frozen member is coordination.price_signal with no edges, so the rule is retained as a non-mathematical procedural coordination rule rather than assigned an unsupported formula. The B evidence remains unreviewed candidate support and is not claimed to have passed source audit.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C001","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C001 is the post-allocation price-responsive purchasing and SES charging/discharging behavior associated with the price-signal coordination function. The frozen graph provides only the unary node coordination.price_signal and no edge for this rule."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R003-C002","node_ids":["coordination.price_signal"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 states the buyer-side price-responsive SES charging/discharging strategy under the condition that the current energy deficit is met. It is bound only to the frozen coordination.price_signal node because the frozen graph has no additional node or edge for this relation."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
